    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133, computed at creation from immutable facts).\n\n**New \u2014 `rest/function/common/Membership.java`**: a shared helper `Membership.levelOf(Owner)` implementing the rule \u2014 start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (leaving level 4 reserved for tenure). Since the inputs (email, namesake count) are frozen at creation, deriving the value at read time yields the same result without a schema change.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: dropped the `membershipTier` mapping (the old GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE expression) and added a `membershipLevel` mapping that delegates to `Membership.levelOf(owner)`.\n\n**`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`**: the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=...` (via the same helper) instead of the tier \u2014 satisfying \"anything that recorded the tier must record the level instead.\"\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`**: replaced the `membershipTier` string property with an integer `membershipLevel` (min 1, max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\nThe four new/changed acceptance tests (Cp15, Cp21, Cp23, Cp24) all pass, confirming: level 3 for a unique owner with email, level 2 for a household member with no email, the audit line records the level, and `membershipTier` no longer exists in the response.",
